[{ "action": "append", "id": "event-modals", "value" : "<div tabindex=\"-1\" id=\"modal-a7565248-dce4-4be4-9355-546c7d4eb17a\" class=\"modal\"><div class=\"modal-dialog modal-lg\"><div class=\"modal-content\"><div class=\"modal-header\"><a data-dismiss=\"modal\" class=\"close\"><span class=\"glyphicon glyphicon-remove\"></span></a><p class=\"text-muted\"><span class=\"glyphicon glyphicon-road\"></span> Research Papers</p><strong>Tue 7 Jul 2026 11:30 - 11:50 at <a href=\"https://conf.researchr.org/room/fse-2026/fse-2026-venue-mb-5.215\" class=\"room-link navigate\">MB 5.215</a></strong> - <a href=\"https://conf.researchr.org/track/fse-2026/fse-2026-research-papers#program\" class=\"navigate\">Program Analysis 1</a> <small>Chair(s): <a href=\"https://conf.researchr.org/profile/fse-2026/martinkellogg\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"navigate\">Martin Kellogg</a></small></div><div class=\"modal-body\"><div class=\"bg-primary event-title\"><h4><span data-event-star=\"a7565248-dce4-4be4-9355-546c7d4eb17a\" title=\"Add event to your program\"><span class=\"text-disabled glyphicon glyphicon-star-empty\"></span></span><strong>JavaScript Pointer Analysis with Adaptive Heap Abstraction</strong></h4></div><div class=\"bg-info event-description\"><p>The conventional approach to represent objects in static program analysis is to use allocation-site abstraction. This design choice may lead to redundant computations when many abstract objects are similar. Existing mechanisms that aim to merge such objects are not effective for JavaScript. We propose a novel adaptive heap abstraction technique that during analysis discovers and merges similar abstract objects, thereby reducing the analysis complexity while preserving most of the precision.</p>\n<p>The technique has been implemented in a state-of-the-art program analyzer for JavaScript. On a collection of 96 challenging programs, it yields a 2X speedup on average (up to 17X) with a negligible loss of precision. The experimental results also show the effects of various analysis configurations.</p>\n<p></p><a href=\"https://cs.au.dk/~amoeller/papers/aha/paper.pdf\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"publication-link navigate\"><span class=\"glyphicon glyphicon-link\"></span> Pre-print</a><p></p><div class=\"row\"><div class=\"col-sm-6\"><a href=\"https://conf.researchr.org/profile/fse-2026/wenyuanxu\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"navigate\"><div class=\"media\"><span class=\"pull-left\"><img alt=\"Wenyuan Xu\" src=\"https://conf.researchr.org/getProfileImage/wenyuanxu/531dc87c-07ec-4716-9e0f-46c853eb0b65/micro-avatar?1784966713000\" class=\"outputimage media-object thumbnail no-bottom-margin\"/></span><div class=\"media-body\"><h5 class=\"media-heading\">Wenyuan Xu<span class=\"pull-right\"><small></small></span></h5><h5 class=\"media-heading\"><span class=\"text-black\">Aarhus University</span></h5></div></div></a></div><div class=\"col-sm-6\"><a href=\"https://conf.researchr.org/profile/fse-2026/andersmoller\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"navigate\"><div class=\"media\"><span class=\"pull-left\"><img alt=\"Anders M&oslash;ller\" src=\"https://conf.researchr.org/getProfileImage/andersmoller/48eeb46b-9bcd-477b-be01-74818f2fdedc/micro-avatar?1784966713000\" class=\"outputimage media-object thumbnail no-bottom-margin\"/></span><div class=\"media-body\"><h5 class=\"media-heading\">Anders M\u00F8ller<span class=\"pull-right\"><small></small></span></h5><h5 class=\"media-heading\"><span class=\"text-black\">Aarhus University</span></h5><h5 class=\"media-heading\"><small>Denmark</small></h5></div></div></a></div></div></div><br></div><div class=\"modal-footer\"><span class=\"pull-left\"><a href=\"https://conf.researchr.org/details/fse-2026/fse-2026-research-papers/104/JavaScript-Pointer-Analysis-with-Adaptive-Heap-Abstraction\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"btn btn-default navigate\"><span class=\"glyphicon glyphicon-new-window\"></span> All Details</a></span><a href=\"#\" data-dismiss=\"modal\" class=\"btn btn-default\"><span class=\"glyphicon glyphicon-remove\"></span> Close</a></div></div></div></div>"},{ "action": "runscript", "value": "$('#modal-a7565248-dce4-4be4-9355-546c7d4eb17a').modal({ backdrop: 'static', keyboard: true}, 'show');" },
